<w:document xmlns:wpc="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingCanvas" xmlns:cx="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/chartex" xmlns:cx1="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2015/9/8/chartex" xmlns:cx2="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2015/10/21/chartex" xmlns:cx3="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2016/5/9/chartex" xmlns:cx4="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2016/5/10/chartex" xmlns:cx5="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2016/5/11/chartex" xmlns:cx6="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2016/5/12/chartex" xmlns:cx7="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2016/5/13/chartex" xmlns:cx8="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2016/5/14/chartex" xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006" xmlns:aink="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2016/ink" xmlns:am3d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2017/model3d" xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:oel="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/2019/extlst" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:m="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/math" xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:wp14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingDrawing" xmlns:wp="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/wordprocessingDrawing" xmlns:w10="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:w14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordml" xmlns:w15="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2012/wordml" xmlns:w16cex="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2018/wordml/cex" xmlns:w16cid="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2016/wordml/cid" xmlns:w16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2018/wordml" xmlns:w16du="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2023/wordml/word16du" xmlns:w16sdtdh="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2020/wordml/sdtdatahash" xmlns:w16sdtfl="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2024/wordml/sdtformatlock" xmlns:w16se="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2015/wordml/symex" xmlns:wpg="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingGroup" xmlns:wpi="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingInk" xmlns:wne="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2006/wordml" xmlns:wps="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingShape" mc:Ignorable="w14 w15 w16se w16cid w16 w16cex w16sdtdh w16sdtfl w16du wp14"><w:body><w:p w14:paraId="480BE2A0" w14:textId="61E45A36" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="00300563"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="120" w:line="276" w:lineRule="auto"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>Our project pairs three lightweight wearable sensor nodes with an offline software “physiological twin” that runs entirely inside the spacecraft. It turns raw body signals, radiation exposure and sleep debt into one clear risk score, explains how that score was reached, and shows which part of the body is under the most strain. No Earth link is needed to detect, understand or react to a developing medical problem.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="224FC690" w14:textId="611B51E2" w:rsidR="00300563" w:rsidRDefault="00300563" w:rsidP="00300563"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>The Problem</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="665D5405" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="00000000" w:rsidP="00300563"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="120" w:line="276" w:lineRule="auto"/><w:ind w:firstLine="720"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>On a Mars mission, Earth is too far to be a first responder. A signal takes up to 22 minutes to arrive, so a call for help and a reply can take 44 minutes or more. For a cardiac event, a radiation-driven crisis or a sudden neurological problem, that gap can decide the outcome.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="256D2081" w14:textId="178BEF53" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="00300563"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="120" w:line="276" w:lineRule="auto"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>Moreover, astronauts are expected to run a mission and also act as their own doctors. In a cramped habitat, with altered gravity, fatigue and a heavy workload, they cannot reliably or regularly assess their own condition, even when diagnostic equipment is on board.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="6684C2C9" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="00000000"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="120" w:line="276" w:lineRule="auto"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve">So the real need is not more medical equipment. It is </w:t></w:r><w:r><w:rPr><w:b/><w:bCs/></w:rPr><w:t>continuous, automatic, local health awareness</w:t></w:r><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve"> that asks nothing of the crew.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="0E3195A1" w14:textId="42A21672" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="00000000"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>Our Solution</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="1F45F797" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="00000000"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="120" w:line="276" w:lineRule="auto"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>We built a two-part system:</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="5A3814E0" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="00000000"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="ListParagraph"/><w:numPr><w:ilvl w:val="0"/><w:numId w:val="2"/></w:numPr><w:spacing w:after="70" w:line="276" w:lineRule="auto"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:b/><w:bCs/></w:rPr><w:t>Hardware:</w:t></w:r><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve"> a tri-node wearable network (head, chest, wrist) that measures continuously and is always ready on the body.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="3485B7FB" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="00000000"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="ListParagraph"/><w:numPr><w:ilvl w:val="0"/><w:numId w:val="2"/></w:numPr><w:spacing w:after="70" w:line="276" w:lineRule="auto"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:b/><w:bCs/></w:rPr><w:t>Software (RCPT):</w:t></w:r><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve"> an offline web application that fuses those signals with radiation and sleep data, scores crew risk in real time, and explains every number.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="08EFF386" w14:textId="3617AF7D" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="00000000"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:before="80" w:after="120"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve">Everything runs locally on the ship. Nothing depends on </w:t></w:r><w:r w:rsidR="000D25A0"><w:t>the signal</w:t></w:r><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve"> to Earth.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="785E1F43" w14:textId="339D1B9B" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="00000000"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>How the System Works</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="4DE24766" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="00000000"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="120" w:line="276" w:lineRule="auto"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:b/><w:bCs/></w:rPr><w:t>Step 1. Sense.</w:t></w:r><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve"> Head and chest nodes capture microvolt-level brain (EEG) and heart (ECG) signals and clean them locally.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="7CD9E9D8" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="00000000"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="120" w:line="276" w:lineRule="auto"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:b/><w:bCs/></w:rPr><w:t>Step 2. Aggregate.</w:t></w:r><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve"> They send compact data packets over Bluetooth Low Energy to the wrist hub, which adds blood pressure, oxygen saturation and in-suit environment readings.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="4EED02D9" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="00000000"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="120" w:line="276" w:lineRule="auto"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:b/><w:bCs/></w:rPr><w:t>Step 3. Transmit.</w:t></w:r><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve"> The wrist hub sends one synchronized telemetry packet through the suit by RF link to the habitat’s local server.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="75931093" w14:textId="0DEED1FF" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="00000000"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="120" w:line="276" w:lineRule="auto"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:b/><w:bCs/></w:rPr><w:t>Step 4. Understand.</w:t></w:r><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve"> RCPT </w:t></w:r><w:r w:rsidR="000D25A0"><w:t xml:space="preserve">software </w:t></w:r><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve">combines the telemetry with radiation dose and sleep </w:t></w:r><w:r w:rsidR="000D25A0"><w:t>debt and</w:t></w:r><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve"> computes a live risk index from 0 to 100.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="25EFDE20" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="00000000"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="120" w:line="276" w:lineRule="auto"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:b/><w:bCs/></w:rPr><w:t>Step 5. Act.</w:t></w:r><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve"> The crew sees the score, the affected organ systems and a plain-language explanation, by screen or by voice, and gets the right alert tier: nominal, elevated or emergency.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="7E293BE0" w14:textId="112D866B" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="00000000"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:lastRenderedPageBreak/><w:t>Hardware: The Tri-Node Wearable System</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="4E412B55" w14:textId="6467D115" w:rsidR="00D56A03" w:rsidRPr="00D56A03" w:rsidRDefault="00D56A03" w:rsidP="00D56A03"><w:r><w:rPr><w:noProof/></w:rPr><w:drawing><wp:inline distT="0" distB="0" distL="0" distR="0" wp14:anchorId="7DCCED10" wp14:editId="4D15B7C1"><wp:extent cx="5731510" cy="3820795"/><wp:effectExtent l="0" t="0" r="2540" b="8255"/><wp:docPr id="2136410129" name="Picture 1"/><wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphicFrameLocks xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" noChangeAspect="1"/></wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphic xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"><a:graphicData uri="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><pic:pic xmlns:pic="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><pic:nvPicPr><pic:cNvPr id="2136410129" name="Picture 2136410129"/><pic:cNvPicPr/></pic:nvPicPr><pic:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId7" cstate="print"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{28A0092B-C50C-407E-A947-70E740481C1C}"><a14:useLocalDpi xmlns:a14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2010/main" val="0"/></a:ext></a:extLst></a:blip><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></pic:blipFill><pic:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="5731510" cy="3820795"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom></pic:spPr></pic:pic></a:graphicData></a:graphic></wp:inline></w:drawing></w:r></w:p><w:p w14:paraId="0EEB00CE" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="00000000"><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="120" w:line="276" w:lineRule="auto"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>Instead of one bulky device, we spread the sensing across three small nodes. Each sits where its signal is strongest, so no single piece is heavy, restrictive or awkward during work or sleep.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:tbl><w:tblPr><w:tblW w:w="9026" w:type="dxa"/><w:tblBorders><w:top w:val="single" w:sz="4" w:space="0" w:color="auto"/><w:left w:val="single" w:sz="4" w:space="0" w:color="auto"/><w:bottom w:val="single" w:sz="4" w:space="0" w:color="auto"/><w:right w:val="single" w:sz="4" w:space="0" w:color="auto"/><w:insideH w:val="single" w:sz="4" w:space="0" w:color="auto"/><w:insideV w:val="single" w:sz="4" w:space="0" w:color="auto"/></w:tblBorders><w:tblCellMar><w:left w:w="10" w:type="dxa"/><w:right w:w="10" w:type="dxa"/></w:tblCellMar><w:tblLook w:val="0000" w:firstRow="0" w:lastRow="0" w:firstColumn="0" w:lastColumn="0" w:noHBand="0" w:noVBand="0"/></w:tblPr><w:tblGrid><w:gridCol w:w="1500"/><w:gridCol w:w="2500"/><w:gridCol w:w="2500"/><w:gridCol w:w="2526"/></w:tblGrid><w:tr w:rsidR="00D372BA" w14:paraId="2064A57B" w14:textId="77777777"><w:trPr><w:tblHeader/></w:trPr><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:w="1500" w:type="dxa"/><w:tcBorders><w:top w:val="single" w:sz="4" w:space="0" w:color="BFC8D4"/><w:left w:val="single" w:sz="4" w:space="0" w:color="BFC8D4"/><w:bottom w:val="single" w:sz="4" w:space="0" w:color="BFC8D4"/><w:right w:val="single" w:sz="4" w:space="0" w:color="BFC8D4"/></w:tcBorders><w:shd w:val="clear" w:color="auto" w:fill="1F3A5F"/><w:tcMar><w:top w:w="80" w:type="dxa"/><w:left w:w="110" w:type="dxa"/><w:bottom w:w="80" w:type="dxa"/><w:right w:w="110" w:type="dxa"/></w:tcMar></w:tcPr><w:p w14:paraId="688A9F32" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="00000000"><w:r><w:rPr><w:b/><w:bCs/><w:color w:val="FFFFFF"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>Node</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:w="2500" w:type="dxa"/><w:tcBorders><w:top w:val="single" w:sz="4" w:space="0" w:color="BFC8D4"/><w:left w:val="single" w:sz="4" w:space="0" w:color="BFC8D4"/><w:bottom w:val="single" w:sz="4" w:space="0" w:color="BFC8D4"/><w:right w:val="single" w:sz="4" w:space="0" w:color="BFC8D4"/></w:tcBorders><w:shd w:val="clear" w:color="auto" w:fill="1F3A5F"/><w:tcMar><w:top w:w="80" w:type="dxa"/><w:left w:w="110" w:type="dxa"/><w:bottom w:w="80" w:type="dxa"/><w:right w:w="110" w:type="dxa"/></w:tcMar></w:tcPr><w:p w14:paraId="290A427E" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="00000000"><w:r><w:rPr><w:b/><w:bCs/><w:color w:val="FFFFFF"/><w:sz w:val="20"/><w:szCs w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t>What it measures</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:w="2500" w:type="dxa"/><w:tcBorders><w:top w:val="single" w:sz="4" w:space="0" w:color="BFC8D4"/><w:left w:val="single" w:sz="4" w:space="0" w:color="BFC8D4"/><w:bottom w:val="single" w:sz="4" w:space="0" w:color="BFC8D4"/><w:right w:val="single" w:sz="4" w:space="0" w:color="BFC8D4"/></w:tcBorders><w:shd w:val="clear" w:color="auto" w:fill="1F3A5F"/><w:tcMar><w:top w:w="80" w:type="dxa"/><w:left w:w="110" w:type="dxa"/><w:bottom w:w="80" w:type="dxa"/><w:right w:w="110" w:type="dxa"/></w:tcMar></w:tcPr><w:p w14:paraId="09A5A2E2" w14:textId="77777777" w:rsidR="00D372BA" w:rsidRDefault="0